//@version=6
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// H Ticks — FVG / iFVG : 15m bias -> 3m inversion -> retest -> decisive 30s inversion -> entry at close ->
//                         stop beyond the retest swing -> fixed 1R with a clear path
//
// REQUIRES A STANDARD 30-SECOND CHART. Anything else shows "Switch to a standard 30-second chart" and generates nothing.
// SEQUENCE (all mechanical, all on confirmed candles; no score, no win-rate claim):
//   1. 15m BIAS: confirmed 15m pivots (2 left / 2 right, strict). A confirmed 15m CLOSE strictly beyond the latest
//      confirmed, still-unbroken swing high (bull) / low (bear) that was available BEFORE the breaking candle began sets the
//      bias. Only newly broken levels are events. Bias = UNKNOWN until the first qualifying break; it then persists until an
//      opposite qualifying break. (Our chosen mechanical definition, not a universal definition of market structure.)
//   2. 3m CONTEXT: a 3m FVG inverts on a confirmed 3m close strictly beyond its far boundary, in the bias direction,
//      inside an enabled entry window. One pending context; a newer eligible one replaces it. Cancelled by a confirmed 3m
//      close back through the zone or by a 15m bias reversal.
//   3. RETEST: a later 30s candle intersects the SAME 3m zone (the inversion candle cannot count). Zone is kept.
//   4. TRIGGER: a fresh 30s FVG (formation candle opens at/after the 3m confirmation, intersects the 3m zone) inverts in the
//      setup direction on a candle strictly after the retest candle, AND that inversion candle is DECISIVE
//      (Standard / Strong preset). A weak inversion never becomes a trigger later.
//   5. ENTRY = that candle's confirmed close. STOP = beyond the observed RETEST-LEG extreme (lowest low / highest high
//      from the first retest candle through the trigger candle) +/- max(1 tick, 0.10 x previous 30s ATR). The old
//      trigger-candle BODY stop NO LONGER EXISTS. TARGET = exactly 1R.
//   6. CLEAR PATH: no opposing 15m/1H/4H gap on [entry, target] AND the target ends >= 1 tick before the nearest unconsumed
//      3m swing level in the target direction. Missing coverage is UNKNOWN, never clear.
//   Gates: same originating window instance, < 3 entries per window instance, no unresolved setup, 15m bias agrees at
//   context creation and at entry. A rejected trigger keeps the context pending and is never re-approved later.
// Timing: all state changes and drawings happen on confirmed 30s bars. Alerts only on confirmed realtime bars.
// Verification: see H_Ticks_FVG_iFVG_NOTES.md (code review + Python model only; NOT compiled in TradingView, NOT Bar-Replay tested).
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// INDICATOR (not a strategy). Outcomes: OPEN / TARGET_HIT / STOP_HIT / AMBIGUOUS on 30s candles strictly AFTER the entry
// candle (opening price first, then the range). No slippage, costs or time exit; an estimate, not broker results.
indicator("H Ticks — FVG / iFVG", shorttitle = "H Ticks", overlay = true, max_boxes_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_bars_back = 500)

const string GRP_GEN = "General"
const string GRP_SET = "Setup"
const string GRP_WIN = "Entry windows (Asia 09:00 Tokyo -> 08:00 London, NY 09:45-11:30, NY 14:30-15:30; DST-aware; Mon-Fri)"
const string GRP_AL  = "Alerts"
string inPreset = input.string("Standard", "Impulse preset (decisive 30s inversion candle)", options = ["Standard", "Strong"], group = GRP_SET, tooltip = "Standard: body >= 0.8 x prev ATR, body/range >= 0.65, close in the outer 20% of the range. Strong: 1.0 x, 0.70, outer 15%. Both: body points in the setup direction and the close extends beyond the trigger gap boundary by max(1 tick, 0.10 x prev ATR). Starting parameters, not optimised or proven.")
int    inMinTick = input.int(1, "Minimum gap size (ticks, all gap sources)", minval = 1, group = GRP_SET, tooltip = "Gaps at least this wide are detected and may form contexts, triggers and obstacles.")
bool   inWinAsia = input.bool(true, "Window A: Asia open -> London open", group = GRP_WIN)
bool   inWinAm = input.bool(true, "Window B: New York morning 09:45-11:30", group = GRP_WIN, tooltip = "Start inclusive, end exclusive. BOTH the 3m context and the entry must belong to the same window instance (max 3 entries per instance, one unresolved setup at a time).")
bool   inWinPm = input.bool(true, "Window C: New York afternoon 14:30-15:30", group = GRP_WIN)
bool   inShowPair = input.bool(true, "Show setup gap pair (3m CONTEXT + 30s TRIGGER)", group = GRP_GEN)
bool   inShowHtf = input.bool(true, "Show nearby HTF gaps", group = GRP_GEN, tooltip = "Display only. Obstacle checks always use ALL tracked 15m/1H/4H gaps, hidden or not.")
bool   inShowRR = input.bool(true, "Show risk/reward shading", group = GRP_GEN)
string inTheme = input.string("Light", "Theme", options = ["Light", "Dark"], group = GRP_GEN, tooltip = "Light: black entry line. Dark: white entry line (black would be invisible).")
bool   inStats = input.bool(true, "Show the five-day results table", group = GRP_GEN)
bool   inStatus = input.bool(true, "Show compact status", group = GRP_GEN)
bool   inDebug = input.bool(false, "Debug: label rejected triggers with the failed gate", group = GRP_GEN)
bool   alEntry = input.bool(true, "Alert on each new entry", group = GRP_AL)
bool   alTarget = input.bool(true, "Alert when a setup hits its target", group = GRP_AL)
bool   alStop = input.bool(true, "Alert when a setup hits its stop", group = GRP_AL)

